WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.600
Inside the program run seven
complementary projects.

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.325
Each has its own charter,
sponsor and success criteria,

3
00:00:07.325 --> 00:00:12.705
and each turns a gap the program often
finds into real work: identity lifecycle,

4
00:00:12.705 --> 00:00:15.602
endpoints, network and access, monitoring,

5
00:00:15.602 --> 00:00:19.575
privileged access, the data
platform, and the supply chain.

6
00:00:19.575 --> 00:00:24.538
Identity goes first, because everything
else uses its attributes and owners.

7
00:00:24.538 --> 00:00:29.775
Privileged access starts early too,
for Tier 0 and emergency access.

8
00:00:29.775 --> 00:00:31.350
And there's a catch worth knowing.

9
00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:36.255
Microsoft recommends at least two cloud-only
emergency accounts with permanent

10
00:00:36.255 --> 00:00:39.356
Global Administrator, so
a target of zero permanent

11
00:00:39.356 --> 00:00:42.313
Global Administrators has
to exempt them by name.

12
00:00:42.313 --> 00:00:44.561
Two source claims have also moved,

13
00:00:44.561 --> 00:00:48.737
around software attestation and
FedRAMP; the notes cover both.

14
00:00:48.737 --> 00:00:53.718
And two rules hold for every project:
none creates a second source of truth,

15
00:00:53.718 --> 00:00:56.412
and none clears a program gate on its own.

16
00:00:56.412 --> 00:00:57.890
So who makes the calls?
